Shared legend: Absolute integration errors on [0,1] versus equal-panel count n (Simpson uses 2n subintervals). Filled symbols are used in the fits (error > 10⁻¹⁵); hollow symbols are excluded. Shading marks errors ≤ 10⁻¹⁵. Downward triangles denote computed zeros, placed at 10⁻¹⁸ for display only; their horizontal positions are slightly offset by method to expose coincident symbols. Dashed lines are slope references with arbitrary vertical offsets, not fitted lines. Errors and n are dimensionless.

1. **exp(x).** Trapezoid and Simpson approach their expected orders; four-node Gauss–Legendre reaches the rounding floor after just two usable points, leaving its regression interval undefined.
2. **1/(1+25x²).** Coarse-panel transients precede the regular decay; all-point fitted orders therefore differ from asymptotic slopes. Gauss–Legendre supplies only four points above the cutoff.
3. **√x.** All methods decay approximately as n⁻³ᐟ², consistent with the nonsmooth endpoint. Its vertical range differs from Figures 1–2 to resolve the three curves; all points are above the fitting cutoff.
